From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:05:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow secondary AP vdev after DFS CAC

ath12k marks every AP vdev start on a radar channel as passive. This is
correct while the channel is in DFS_USABLE state and CAC is still required,
but not after CAC has changed the channel to DFS_AVAILABLE.

This matters when multiple AP BSSes share a channel context. mac80211 starts
the first BSS after CAC, then starts each additional BSS vdev in turn. The
firmware rejects the later passive vdev start while the radio is already
beaconing, causing NL80211_CMD_START_AP to fail.

Set the passive flag for a radar channel only while CAC is required. Keep the
DFS flags unchanged so radar detection remains enabled on the channel context,
and preserve NO_IR handling for non-radar channels.

Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -10628,7 +10628,8 @@ ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart(struct ath
 
 		arg.freq2_radar = ctx->radar_enabled;
 
-		arg.passive = arg.chan_radar;
+		arg.passive = arg.chan_radar &&
+			cfg80211_chandef_dfs_usable(hw->wiphy, chandef);
 
 		spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 		arg.regdomain = ar->ab->dfs_region;
@@ -10637,7 +10639,8 @@ ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart(struct ath
 		/* TODO: Notify if secondary 80Mhz also needs radar detection */
 	}
 
-	arg.passive |= !!(chandef->chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IR);
+	if (!arg.chan_radar)
+		arg.passive = !!(chandef->chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IR);
 
 	if (!restart)
 		ath12k_mac_mlo_get_vdev_args(arvif, &arg.ml);
